<title>USA: Patriot buys hotels in Chicago, Nashville.</title>
<headline>Patriot buys hotels in Chicago, Nashville.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Patriot American Hospitality Inc said Thursday it has completed its acquisition of the 219-room Ambassador West Hotel in Chicago for $15.75 million and the 124-room Union Station Hotel in Nashville for $9.7 million, both for cash.</p>
<p>The company said that the two hotels will be leased to, and managed by, Patriot's newly formed paired operating company, following the completion of the acquisition of Grand Heritage Hotels Inc, which formerly owned and currently manages them both.</p>
<p>Patriot American is a paired hotel real-estate investment trust, which can both own and operate its hotel properties.</p>
</text>
